,"requests":1},"project.symbol-reference-completeness":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":45555.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":1821.0,"requests":4}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify which emitter serializes the WHOLE file on --write (a single emitter that handles both flat sections and nested [mapping.*] tables), so the read-whole/re-emit round-trip preserves sibling [jira]/[tracker] sections without tripping _emit_toml's nested-table guard.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["_config_writer.py:188 re-emits the whole file: 'text = _emit_toml(data)'","_emit_toml raises ConfigError on any nested sub-table (_config_writer.py:83-87)","plan: '_emit_nested_toml ... used ONLY for [mapping.*]; _emit_toml and its pinned test are left as-is'","plan: '--write: mirror write_jira_config's read-whole/mutate/re-emit/atomic-replace pattern'"],"finding":"The --write mechanism reuses write_jira_config's read-whole/mutate/re-emit-WHOLE-file pattern, but that pattern serializes the entire file through a SINGLE emitter (_emit_toml at _config_writer.py:188). The plan scopes _emit_nested_toml to '[mapping.*] ONLY' and leaves _emit_toml as-is, leaving unresolved which emitter serializes the WHOLE file when the target rebar.toml contains flat sibling sections ([jira]/[tracker]) alongside the new nested [mapping.*]. _emit_toml fail-closes on the nested [mapping] table, and a mapping-only helper must still round-trip the flat sibling sections it did not author.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa832ff0f9288e7a8","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Serialization (concrete)' and 'Emit: --write'","norm_id":"nb3292e281db36dc1","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["--write against an existing rebar.toml that already has a [jira] section: whole-file re-emit hits _emit_toml's nested guard on [mapping] and aborts, or the mapping-only helper drops/mis-emits [jira]"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Have _emit_nested_toml serialize the ENTIRE mutated dict (flat top-level keys + one-level [section] tables + recursed [section.sub] tables) and use it as the sole whole-file emitter on the --write path, rather than mixing it with _emit_toml; keep _emit_toml (and its pinned test) untouched for the [jira] onboarding path only.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an AC exercising the fake port returning empty results and/or raising (unknown KEY, unreachable Jira) to assert the command's error/empty-state behavior.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.075,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["ACs cover only test_probe_emits_mapping, test_probe_is_read_only, test_probe_write_preserves_edits, test_probe_transitions_best_effort.","No AC drives an empty getter, a raising port, or an unknown-KEY path through the emitter/handler."],"finding":"The four ACs are all happy-path/partial-data variants against the fake port (emit, read-only, write-preserves-edits, transitions-best-effort). None exercises an error or empty state: no test for an invalid project KEY, a probe-port getter raising/returning empty, or a Jira-unreachable failure. For a new user-facing CLI flow, the failure/empty paths are untested.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f96ebf26a52af7b31","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n46f42e58ba2b382d","priority":0.875,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A regression that crashes on an empty issue_types() list or a nonexistent KEY ships green because no AC covers it."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add e.g. test_probe_empty_or_unreachable: fake port returns empty vocab or raises; assert an actionable error / empty-block-with-note and no partial/garbage file write.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the baseline citation to name `_map_local_to_jira_fields` (the function at outbound_fields.py:140-158) rather than `map_local_to_remote` (the backend.py:73 port wrapper).","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0389,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"the outbound create path `adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:140-158` (`map_local_to_remote`)\"","outbound_fields.py:101 defines `def _map_local_to_jira_fields(...)`; the summary/description/issuetype/priority/assignee dict is at lines 140-146 with conditional status (150-151) and parent (152+)","backend.py:73 is where `map_local_to_remote` (the port method) lives, delegating to `_map_local_to_jira_fields`"],"finding":"The AC 'create_defaults baseline' cites `map_local_to_remote` at `adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:140-158`, but the function actually defined at those lines is `_map_local_to_jira_fields`; `map_local_to_remote` is the backend port method (jira/backend.py:73) that delegates to it. The cited lines and field baseline are correct, but the function name at that location is wrong.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"faa551739e07d8955","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria / 'create_defaults baseline (concrete)' paragraph","norm_id":"n76b547c1ca601784","priority":0.6611,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer greps `outbound_fields.py` for `map_local_to_remote` and finds nothing, wasting time reconciling the citation"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Change '(`map_local_to_remote`)' to '(`_map_local_to_jira_fields`)' in the create_defaults baseline paragraph, or note that `map_local_to_remote` (backend.py) delegates to `_map_local_to_jira_fields` at the cited lines.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the probe's behavior when a per-axis live call fails or returns empty (surface a per-axis note/warning and emit that layer empty, rather than crashing the whole command), so partial failures are visible and non-fatal.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3637,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan enumerates many live jira.JIRA calls but states failure handling only for 'transition hints (best-effort)' and hierarchy ('DROPPED ... not fabricated')","No mention of timeout / connection-failure / auth-failure behavior for the probe's read calls"],"finding":"The probe issues live pycontribs read calls (issue_types, priorities, statuses, createmeta_*, search_issues, transitions) but the plan does not specify error handling when a call fails, times out, or returns empty — no graceful-degradation, surfaced-error, or partial-emit behavior is stated for the read path (only transitions are flagged best-effort).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f32f742ac164d3c4b","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach 'Probe' / 'Axis grounding' section","norm_id":"n08c0347596215db8","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Jira is down or slow when running suggest-mapping","createmeta endpoint disabled/forbidden for the project","priorities()/statuses() raises a pycontribs exception mid-probe"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Adopt the same 'drop + emit empty + note' pattern already stated for hierarchy across all axes: on a failed/empty per-axis call, emit that layer empty with a comment naming the failure, and continue.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify the probe's degrade-on-failure/empty contract per axis (createmeta permission error, empty vocab, no search_issues sample), so a failed or empty getter drops that axis with an honest note rather than crashing or emitting a silently-empty block.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0137,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["plan handles only the hierarchyLevel-absent case ('DROPPED (emitted empty + note), not fabricated')","no mention of createmeta permission errors or empty-vocabulary projects","createmeta_issuetypes/createmeta_fieldtypes commonly 403 without project-admin scope"],"finding":"The probe's failure/empty edge cases are unspecified: createmeta calls can raise on insufficient permission, and priorities()/statuses()/issue_types()/search_issues() can legitimately return empty for a sparse project. The plan does not state how the probe degrades (skip axis + honest note vs. abort vs. emit empty block) when a getter fails or returns nothing.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f520651b2fc8af6cc","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Axis grounding' and AC test_probe_emits_mapping","norm_id":"nd2112507d3de3627","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Running suggest-mapping against a project where the credential lacks createmeta permission","An empty/newly-created project with no priorities configured or no sample issues for transitions"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify command behavior for invalid/nonexistent project KEY, unreachable-Jira / missing-credential failures, and empty vocabulary results (error vs. empty-block-with-note), not just the partial-data cases.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["T6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4475,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan handles 'If hierarchyLevel is absent, the hierarchy axis is DROPPED', transitions 'flagged best-effort', global statuses 'documents that honest limitation' — but no mention of connection/auth failure, invalid project KEY, or empty getters.","'Default port built from build_client_from_settings' — a live network/credential boundary whose failure mode is unstated."],"finding":"The plan does not specify behavior for the highest-stakes live-probe error states: a nonexistent/invalid project KEY (createmeta returns nothing), an unreachable Jira or missing/invalid credentials from build_client_from_settings, and empty vocabulary results (e.g. issue_types() returns []). Only partial-data cases (absent hierarchyLevel, partial transitions, global statuses) are addressed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2898fa0ca9167fdb","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Probe section","norm_id":"n2a325662b9d2a93e","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A user runs `rebar bridge suggest-mapping WRONGKEY` and createmeta returns nothing → unclear whether the command errors, emits an empty block, or crashes.","Jira is unreachable or credentials are stale → the command surfaces an unhandled exception rather than an actionable error."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add an explicit error/empty-state contract: on connection/auth failure emit an actionable error and non-zero exit; on an unknown project KEY fail closed with a clear message; on empty getters emit the layer empty with a note rather than crashing.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State explicitly whether the stdout block and the --write target use the same table prefix (reconcile `[tool.rebar.mapping]` vs `[mapping.projects.<KEY>]`) so AC1 and the --write path name the same entity.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.615,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'emits a `[tool.rebar.mapping]` block'","Emit: 'build `{\"projects\": {<KEY>: {<layer>}}}`'","--write: 'DEEP-MERGE under `[mapping.projects.<KEY>]`'","Context lists both '`[mapping]` / `[tool.rebar.mapping]`' as the reserved block"],"finding":"AC1 names the emitted block `[tool.rebar.mapping]` while the --write path and Emit section place data under `[mapping.projects.<KEY>]`; the plan uses two different table prefixes (`tool.rebar.mapping` vs `mapping.projects`) without stating whether stdout and --write emit the same prefix.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdd171565533527a1","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria AC1 vs Approach 'Emit' / '--write' bullets","norm_id":"nd10e39beb8449ae1","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor emits stdout under one prefix and writes under another, producing config that mapping_config.py (S1) does not parse"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Pick one canonical prefix (matching what mapping_config.py parses in S1) and use it uniformly in AC1, the Emit bullet, and the --write bullet.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.85,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile parent epic 3d7a AC #8 / child-decomposition S8 wording (`rebar bridge probe`) with the leaf's renamed verb `rebar bridge suggest-mapping`, so the parent's named deliverable matches what S8 ships.","cohort":["G7"],"criteria":["G7"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.52,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent AC #8: 'A `rebar bridge probe` command interrogates a live target and emits suggested config for every offline-discoverable axis, flagging transitions as best-effort'","Parent child decomposition: 'S8 — `rebar bridge probe` command interrogates a live target and emits suggested config'","Leaf: 'New verb: **`rebar bridge suggest-mapping`**' — justified because 'Verb `rebar bridge probe` COLLIDES with the retired alias `bridge-probe`' which is not read-only","Functional contract (interrogate live target, emit suggested config for offline-discoverable axes, flag transitions best-effort) is preserved faithfully; only the verb name differs — a wording-level mismatch, not a contract contradiction"],"finding":"Leaf S8 renames the parent's named deliverable `rebar bridge probe` (parent AC #8 and child-decomposition S8 line) to `rebar bridge suggest-mapping`; the parent's verb name is not reconciled to the renamed verb.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd8a98443ebc688f6","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"S8 plan Context/Approach (verb `rebar bridge suggest-mapping`) vs parent 3d7a AC #8 and child decomposition line 'S8 — rebar bridge probe command'","norm_id":"n5de93fe31d6d29f5","priority":0.33,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reader cross-checking the parent's AC #8 against the shipped verb finds `bridge probe` in the epic but `bridge suggest-mapping` in the command"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Update parent 3d7a AC #8 and the S8 child-decomposition line to name `rebar bridge suggest-mapping` (noting the `bridge-probe` alias collision as rationale), which re-triggers the parent's plan-review; the leaf itself already documents the rename correctly.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the createmeta-driven create_defaults stubs with the documented out-of-scope decision at docs/user-guide.md:621-629 — either state explicitly why emitting human-fillable config stubs is distinct from the rejected write-time createmeta pre-flight, or drop the createmeta axis.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["docs/user-guide.md:621-624: 'A createmeta pre-flight is deliberately out of scope, and that is the mature answer rather than a gap. Jira's /rest/api/2/issue/createmeta can enumerate a project's required fields, so an obvious-looking fix is to query it and populate whatever it reports. rebar does not...'","docs/user-guide.md:624-628 cites Sentry precedent that a sync bridge cannot invent a meaningful value for an arbitrary required custom field","Plan does not mention this documented boundary or explain why suggest-mapping's createmeta use (emitting fillable stubs into config) is distinct from the rejected write-time pre-flight"],"finding":"The plan's create_defaults axis is populated via createmeta_issuetypes/createmeta_fieldtypes, but the codebase documents an explicit, reasoned decision that a createmeta pre-flight is deliberately out of scope (docs/user-guide.md:621-629, citing the Sentry precedent that a sync bridge cannot invent meaningful values for arbitrary required custom fields). The plan neither cites nor reconciles with this decision-of-record.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd61238a59496ee08","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'create_defaults stubs → jira.JIRA.createmeta_issuetypes(<KEY>) + createmeta_fieldtypes(...)'; AC 'create_defaults baseline (concrete)'","norm_id":"nbfeeae9ccc47c4be","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer or maintainer sees a new createmeta consumer that appears to reverse a documented, precedent-backed out-of-scope decision","The suggested config auto-lists required custom fields as stubs, re-opening the exact 'guessing custom-required-field values' surface the docs say rebar deliberately refuses"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a sentence to the Approach/AC explaining that suggest-mapping only EMITS a create_defaults stub into a config file for a human to fill (never auto-invents a write value at reconcile time), which is orthogonal to the write-time createmeta pre-flight rebar declines in docs/user-guide.md:621-629; or, if that distinction does not hold, remove createmeta from the axis set and note create_defaults is left empty for the operator.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Classify the four vocabulary getters (issue_types/priorities/issue_link_types/statuses) as UNVERIFIED external surfaces and either cite the pycontribs 3.8–4 API doc/signature confirming each, or route a short live-smoke/spike to observe their real method names and return shapes before committing.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the vocabulary getters are documented pycontribs 3.x public API for that client' — asserted, not observed","search_files for issue_types(, issue_link_types, .statuses( found NO in-repo call to these jira.JIRA getters (only acli_graph.get_issue_link_types, a different surface)","resolve_symbol('jira.JIRA') → UNRESOLVED in this environment (not proof of absence, but the method surface is unverified here)","Contrast: search_issues and transitions() ARE confirmed in-repo (transitions.py:80; dozens of DC-adapter uses)"],"finding":"The plan's core vocabulary axes depend on pycontribs jira.JIRA methods (issue_types(), priorities(), issue_link_types(), statuses()) that are used NOWHERE in the repo and could not be resolved in this environment; the plan asserts they are 'documented pycontribs 3.x public API' but names no verification step or spike.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fed4332ba9491ab97","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Axis grounding' bullets; Pin jira>=3.8,<4 (pyproject.toml:202)","norm_id":"n0f6a2dcd85611814","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A method name or return-shape mismatch (e.g. statuses() returning Status objects vs project-scoped list, or a renamed getter across the >=3.8,<4 r